 -- BUILD+LAUNCH (operator TOP PRIORITY 2026-06-11; G1; split-long-codex BUILD
 half): write the standalone two-arm + positive-control runner that measures
 whether the SAME GAP-4 execution-consistency primitive transfers to CODE.
 Reuse the DOMAIN-GENERAL primitives (python/carnot/verify/sandbox.py
 restricted exec + the demo-fit/content-hash logic in
 python/carnot/agentic/arc_gap4_execution_verifier.py) -- do NOT write a
 code-specific verifier; the whole point is the primitive is SHARED. Corpus:
 MBPP (and/or HumanEval); visible example tests = the 'demos', hidden tests =
 held-out 'gold'. Smoke on 2 tasks, commit the runner, then LAUNCH the full
 run BACKGROUNDED (the run makes N>=30 x k>=8 local-GGUF generations and must
 not hold an agent past the 80-min cap).

